namespace test.voidcollide
version "1.0.0"

// v3.2 seat 9 round 1 (F8 / D47 - the code-quality review's SF-8): a MODEL-DECLARED basic type whose NAME collides with
// a builtin. The fork's ONE law (`BuiltinTypeRegistry.basicOrRecordNodeType`: a registered twin for a builtins-model
// declaration, `nothing` for a model-declared one) is a NAME lookup, so this declaration would resolve to the BUILTIN
// `string` - the third case its javadoc did not name. The released plugin's verdict decides: a refusal (a duplicate
// declaration) or goldens. Kept apart so a plugin refusal costs one group.

basicType string <"A model-declared basic type named like the builtin.">

type Carrier: <"An attribute typed by the colliding declaration.">
    s string (0..1)
